      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: [Build 1392]\n\nHey!\n\nI'll answer in the order of paragraphs in the post (since this annoyingly contains multiple issues):\n\nLoading screen thumbnails show up fine. They are perhaps a little closer to the ground and nearer to me than on PC, though.\n\nThe avatar hands are still misaligned with the controllers, in my experience exactly as shown in the post's images. This means if I touch the base of the controllers together the hands end up inside each other.\n\nI don't have a Quest to compare performance, but I would expect the home world should run at a stable 72fps with a decently optimised avatar, ranked Good/Medium, though I do get 72-90 on average, it drops as I walk around the home world. It drops to 55-60 with the mirror enabled on half resolution, and then opening the menu tanks that down to 35fps. (looking at the graphs, it's GPU-bound, but the CPU doesn't have much headroom either.)\n\nI cannot check the \"doubled\" own nametag as my right eye is kinda trash, but this is the first time I've heard of it.\n\nAll mobile platforms appear as Android now. As much as I'd like specific platform tags (Quest, Mobile, Pico, HTC, etc), the OS tag serves its purpose perfectly.\n\nResolution still seems to be lower than native, though with the current state of performance I doubt increasing it is a good idea.\n\nSo, to summarise the issues that remain:\n\n- Misaligned avatar hands\n\n- Low performance even in default home with Medium/Good avatars.\n\n- Resolution seems lower than native.\n\nI'm happy to test things if needed/possible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
