      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}\n\nAs of Build 1435, which just got released on Pico, it seems now the -controller- offsets are broken, but in the opposite direction; the in-game model is too far forward.\n\nIt's like, the avatar hands are now in-line with the in-game render model, but the render model has also been moved forward.\n\nI feel like the avatar hands are pitched a little too far up. The fingers should be closer to the handle. If I remember correctly about a 20 degree wrist angle offset prior to this update made it feel right angle-wise.\n\nThey look to be about the same distance as before, see:\n\nhttps://youtube.com/shorts/TVpc1-cWkOI \n\n(annoyingly, YT made it into a short because it's square)\n\nI've only played once since the update, I'll report back if there's any change from this state.",
