  "details": "- Loading screens are still broken on Pico. You cannot even see the world image. It's one big white block. This must fixed because it's very ugly view.\n\n- Second, the Pico Controllers don't align correctly on hands. They're a bit off, more forward. Pointing is still oke, it's just weird to see it. Need adjust it.\n\n(!) I know Pico4 has higher clocked chip, but it has bit worser FPS result compared to Quest 2. Hope next Pico builds will more optimized for it. Thanks to bigger memory, worlds are more smooth to rotate around. I will do more FPS tests with my headsets (P4-Q2-Q3 in home) so i can find out what is not well optimized.\n\n- Your own name tag is kinda weird in 3D, its not correct rendered so you see sort of \"double\" tag. It's not pleasant view with \"wrong\" 3D view. Normal player name tags are fine, it's just your own name tag is bit weird. Name tag in Q2/Q3 are fine.\n\n- It has still Quest tag, while you have made for Mobile version own tag. So we should have own Pico tag for it. Not a bug, just mention it.\n\nGood start for Pico, world loading are fine, but it's on Quest 2 level, so sharpness is not there. (Quest 3 is way much sharper), so in graphic wise, hope this can better because Pico can bit more than Quest 2.",
